SizeRank":31,"finishersRank":36,"finishRateRank":85,"winningTimeRank":25,"winningTimeRankDir":8,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2002 Comrades Marathon was the 77th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.550 km. The race was held on Monday, 17 June. Conditions: Cool at start. Mild to warm. Never oppressively hot. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nVladimir KOTOV claimed the men's title in 05:30:59, ahead of Willie Mtolo (05:33:35) and Jorge Martinez (05:33:37). Maria BAK won the women's race in 06:14:21, followed by Natalia VOLGINA (06:17:26).\n\nMaria BAK's 06:14:21 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 12,155 entries, 9,019 runners crossed the finish line (74.2% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 7,831 men and 1,188 women (13.2% female). The average finish time was 09:37:54.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 564 Silver, 2,204 Bill Rowan, 6,231 Bronze. 1,537 runners (17.0%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Daniel MCNAMARA in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 2000, the field was 50.4% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 44% of the finishers, with 5,066 seniors (avg 09:28:54) and 3,953 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}